    "title": "Wet roads bring unusual traffic on Beaumont highways - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bianca Thomas ,\n6 hours ago Cars drive through wet roads in this Enterprise archive photo. (Kim Brent) Today's traffic is once again delayed by rainy weather.\nDrivers on U.S. 69 northbound may face some stop-and-go traffic once they reach FM 3514. According to the Texas Department of Transportation traffic maps and cameras, this traffic continues down U.S. 69 past Lamar University. It continues on the Interstate 10 interchange near Corporate Drive and Washington Boulevard.\nTraffic picks up again and continues down I-10 westbound. According to TxDOT, the heavy traffic continues past College Street and U.S. 90. Traffic clears and begins moving freely near Hollywood Avenue and Hollywood Street, but picks back up on I-10 near Rusk Street and continues until the I-10 and U.S. 69 interchange near Louisiana Street.\nDrivers on I-10 westbound coming from Vidor and Rose City can expect some traffic near the Neches River. The congestion continues down the I-10 and U.S. 90 interchange at Pine Street and goes past Babe Zaharias Park. Traffic begins moving freely on the I-10 and U.S. 69 interchange near Toccoa Street.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com",
